          <p>Promoting digital education, cabinet minister BD Kalla on Monday inaugurated the state-wide implementation of Mission Buniyaad, which aims to provide quality education through the digital medium. The initiative was being run in six districts of the state for the past six months, which will now cover all districts and around 20 lakh students will get the benefits, said officials.</p>
          <p>Mission Buniyaad is one of the initiatives that focuses on recouping learning level loss due to the pandemic.</p>
          <p>On Monday, the state-wide implementation was announced by BD Kalla, Zahida Khan, minister of state for education and other officials.</p>
          <p>Officials said that the pilot project was conducted among 35,000 girl students in six districts - Udaipur, Bhilwara, Sikar, Karauli, Dhaulpur, and Sirohi, where an average learning outcome improvement of 16% between baseline and end line was noted.</p>
          <p>"The six-month pilot included students from class 8-12 spending two hours per week on digital devices for personalized and adaptive learning (PAL) and in-person school instruction. The road map for Mission Buniyaad targets improvements across all three pillars of digital education - Access, Equity, and Quality. The PAL platform backtracks on a student's progression to cover every possible gap in learning," said officials.</p>

